-   "source": "## 8 — Materialise the prompt set\n\nThe spec above is the *recipe*; this step expands it into the actual **list of generation calls** and writes them to `prompts.jsonl` (one JSON object per line) under `WORK_DIR/data/processed/`.\n\nKeeping prompt *construction* (here, CPU-only, seconds) separate from prompt *execution* (nb03, GPU-bound, possibly hours) buys two things:\n\n- **Resumability.** Each call carries a deterministic `job_id` (hash of kind + spec + emotion + topic). nb03 skips any `job_id` already present in its output, so an interrupted Colab session — or a pre-empted HPC job — just picks up where it left off.\n- **Portability.** `prompts.jsonl` is a self-contained, model-agnostic job manifest. Build it once on Drive (or locally), then point an HPC run at the same file with `EMOVEC_WORK_DIR=…` — no need to re-run the whole notebook on the cluster.\n\nEach record holds: `kind` (`emotion_story` / `neutral_dialogue` / `emotional_dialogue`), the fully-rendered `system_prompt`, the `user` trigger, expected `n_outputs`, a per-call `seed`, and provenance (`spec_hash`, `generator_model`).",
+   "source": "## 8 \u2014 Materialise the prompt set\n\nThe spec above is the *recipe*; this step expands it into the actual **list of generation calls** and writes them to `prompts.jsonl` (one JSON object per line) under `WORK_DIR/data/processed/`.\n\nKeeping prompt *construction* (here, CPU-only, seconds) separate from prompt *execution* (nb03, GPU-bound, possibly hours) buys two things:\n\n- **Resumability.** Each call carries a deterministic `job_id` (hash of kind + spec + emotion + topic). nb03 skips any `job_id` already present in its output, so an interrupted Colab session \u2014 or a pre-empted HPC job \u2014 just picks up where it left off.\n- **Portability.** `prompts.jsonl` is a self-contained, model-agnostic job manifest. Build it once on Drive (or locally), then point an HPC run at the same file with `EMOVEC_WORK_DIR=\u2026` \u2014 no need to re-run the whole notebook on the cluster.\n\nEach record holds: `kind` (`emotion_story` / `neutral_dialogue` / `emotional_dialogue`), the fully-rendered `system_prompt`, the `user` trigger, expected `n_outputs`, a per-call `seed`, and provenance (`spec_hash`, `generator_model`).",
